              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "I say that the hexagon {ABCDEF|hexagon} is equilateral and equiangular.",
              visible: HEX,
              highlighted: ["hexagon"] },
            { text: "For, since the point {G} is the center of the circle {ABCDEF|ABCDEFc}, {GE} equals {GD}.",
              visible: HEX,
              highlighted: ["G","ABCDEFc","EG","DG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "radii of the circle ABCDEF", ref: "I.Def.15" }] },
            { text: "Again, since the point {D} is the center of the circle {GCH}, {DE} equals {DG}.",
              visible: HEX,
              highlighted: ["D","EGCH","DE","DG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "radii of the circle GCH", ref: "I.Def.15" }] },
            { text: "But {GE} was proved equal to {GD}, therefore {GE} also equals {ED}.",
              visible: HEX,
              highlighted: ["EG","DG","DE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "each equals GD", ref: "C.N.1" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the triangle {EGD} is equilateral,",
              visible: TRI,
              highlighted: ["EGD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "EGD", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] } },
            { text: "and therefore its three angles {EGD|angEGD}, {GDE}, and {DEG} equal one another,",
              visible: TANG,
              highlighted: ["angEGD","angGDE","angDEG"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angEGD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angGDE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angDEG", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "inasmuch as, in isosceles triangles, the angles at the base equal one another.",
              visible: TANG,
              highlighted: ["EGD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.5" }] },
            { text: "And the sum of the three angles of the triangle equals two right angles,",
              visible: TANG,
              highlighted: ["angEGD","angGDE","angDEG"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.32" }] },
            { text: "therefore the angle {EGD|angEGD} is one-third of two right angles.",
              visible: TANG,
              highlighted: ["angEGD"] },
            { text: "Similarly, the angle {DGC} can also be proved to be one third of two right angles.",
              visible: CEN2,
              highlighted: ["angDGC"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angDGC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "And, since the straight line {CG} standing on {EB}",
              visible: CEN2,
              highlighted: ["CG","EB"] },
            { text: "makes the sum of the adjacent angles {EGC} and {CGB} equal to two right angles,",
              visible: ADJ,
              highlighted: ["angEGC","angCGB"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angEGC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angCGB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angles EGC and CGB on the straight line EB", ref: "I.13" }] },
            { text: "therefore the remaining angle {CGB} is also one-third of two right angles.",
              visible: CEN3,
              highlighted: ["angCGB"] },
            { text: "Therefore the angles {EGD|angEGD}, {DGC}, and {CGB} equal one another,",
              visible: CEN3,
              highlighted: ["angEGD","angDGC","angCGB"] },
            { text: "so that the angles vertical to them, the angles {BGA}, {AGF}, and {FGE}, are equal.",
              visible: VERT,
              highlighted: ["angBGA","angAGF","angFGE"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angBGA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angAGF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angFGE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "vertical angles are equal", ref: "I.15" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the six angles {EGD|angEGD}, {DGC}, {CGB}, {BGA}, {AGF}, and {FGE} equal one another.",
              visible: VERT,
              highlighted: ["angEGD","angDGC","angCGB","angBGA","angAGF","angFGE"] },
            { text: "But equal angles stand on equal circumferences,",
              visible: VERT,
              highlighted: ["angEGD","angDGC","angCGB","angBGA","angAGF","angFGE"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "III.26" }] },
            { text: "therefore the six circumferences {AB|arcAB}, {BC|arcBC}, {CD|arcCD}, {DE|arcDE}, {EF|arcEF}, and {FA|arcFA} equal one another.",
              visible: ARCS,
              highlighted: ["arcAB","arcBC","arcCD","arcDE","arcEF","arcFA"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "arcAB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "arcBC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "arcCD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "arcDE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "arcEF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "arcFA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "And straight lines that cut off equal circumferences are equal, therefore the six straight lines equal one another.",
              visible: ARCS,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC","CD","DE","EF","FA"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "III.29" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the hexagon {ABCDEF|hexagon} is equilateral.",
              visible: HEX,
              highlighted: ["hexagon"] },
            { text: "I say next that it is also equiangular.",
              visible: HEX,
              highlighted: ["hexagon"] },
            { text: "For, since the circumference {FA|arcFA} equals the circumference {ED|arcDE},",
              visible: EQA,
              highlighted: ["arcFA","arcDE"] },
            { text: "add the circumference {ABCD} to each,",
              visible: ADD,
              highlighted: ["ABCD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "ABCD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "therefore the whole {FABCD} equals the whole {EDCBA}.",
              visible: WHOLE,
              highlighted: ["FABCD","EDCBA"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "FABCD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "EDCBA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "equals added to equals", ref: "C.N.2" }] },
            { text: "And the angle {FED} stands on the circumference {FABCD},",
              visible: STAND,
              highlighted: ["angFED","FABCD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angFED", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "and the angle {AFE} on the circumference {EDCBA},",
              visible: STAND2,
              highlighted: ["angAFE","EDCBA"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angAFE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "therefore the angle {AFE} equals the angle {DEF}.",
              visible: STAND2,
              highlighted: ["angAFE","angFED"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "angles on equal circumferences", ref: "III.27" }] },
            { text: "Similarly it can be proved that the remaining angles of the hexagon {ABCDEF|hexagon}",
              visible: ALLANG,
              highlighted: ["angA","angB","angC","angD"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "are also severally equal to each of the angles {AFE} and {FED},",
              visible: ALLANG,
              highlighted: ["angA","angB","angC","angD","angAFE","angFED"] },
            { text: "therefore the hexagon {ABCDEF|hexagon} is equiangular.",
              visible: ALLANG,
              highlighted: ["angA","angB","angC","angD","angAFE","angFED"] },
            { text: "But it was also proved equilateral, and it has been inscribed in the circle {ABCDEF|ABCDEFc}.",
              visible: HEX,
              highlighted: ["hexagon"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "each angle lies on the circumference", ref: "IV.Def.3" }] },
            { text: "Therefore an equilateral and equiangular hexagon has been inscribed in the given circle.",
              visible: HEX,
              highlighted: ["hexagon","ABCDEFc"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.F." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "IV.15") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Def.15": "/elements/books/bookI/definitions/defI15/",
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.Post.2": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post2/",
        "I.Post.3": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post3/",
        "C.N.1":    "/elements/books/bookI/commonnotions/cn1/",
        "C.N.2":    "/elements/books/bookI/commonnotions/cn2/",
        "I.5":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI5/",
        "I.13":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI13/",
        "I.15":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI15/",
        "I.32":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI32/",
        "III.1":    "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII1/",
        "III.26":   "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII26/",
        "III.27":   "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII27/",
        "III.29":   "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII29/",
        "IV.Def.3": "/elements/books/bookIV/definitions/defIV3/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

For, since the point {G} is the center of the circle {ABCDEF|ABCDEFc}, {GE} equals {GD}.

Again, since the point {D} is the center of the circle {GCH}, {DE} equals {DG}.

But {GE} was proved equal to {GD}, therefore {GE} also equals {ED}.  Therefore the triangle {EGD} is equilateral, and therefore its three angles {EGD|angEGD}, {GDE}, and {DEG} equal one another, inasmuch as, in isosceles triangles, the angles at the base equal one another. [!just I.5]

And the sum of the three angles of the triangle equals two right angles, therefore the angle {EGD|angEGD} is one-third of two right angles. [!just I.32]

Similarly, the angle {DGC} can also be proved to be one third of two right angles.

And, since the straight line {CG} standing on {EB} makes the sum of the adjacent angles {EGC} and {CGB} equal to two right angles, therefore the remaining angle {CGB} is also one-third of two right angles. [!just I.13]

Therefore the angles {EGD|angEGD}, {DGC}, and {CGB} equal one another, so that the angles vertical to them, the angles {BGA}, {AGF}, and {FGE}, are equal. [!just I.15]

Therefore the six angles {EGD|angEGD}, {DGC}, {CGB}, {BGA}, {AGF}, and {FGE} equal one another.

But equal angles stand on equal circumferences, therefore the six circumferences {AB|arcAB}, {BC|arcBC}, {CD|arcCD}, {DE|arcDE}, {EF|arcEF}, and {FA|arcFA} equal one another. [!just III.26]

And straight lines that cut off equal circumferences are equal, therefore the six straight lines equal one another.  Therefore the hexagon {ABCDEF|hexagon} is equilateral. [!just III.29]

I say next that it is also equiangular.

For, since the circumference {FA|arcFA} equals the circumference {ED|arcDE}, add the circumference {ABCD} to each, therefore the whole {FABCD} equals the whole {EDCBA}.  And the angle {FED} stands on the circumference {FABCD}, and the angle {AFE} on the circumference {EDCBA}, therefore the angle {AFE} equals the angle {DEF}. [!just III.27]

Similarly it can be proved that the remaining angles of the hexagon {ABCDEF|hexagon} are also severally equal to each of the angles {AFE} and {FED}, therefore the hexagon {ABCDEF|hexagon} is equiangular.

But it was also proved equilateral, and it has been inscribed in the circle {ABCDEF|ABCDEFc}.

Therefore an equilateral and equiangular hexagon has been inscribed in the given circle.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
